# Third-party licence notice — privacy-sidecar

The sidecar's own source (`src/`, `CMakeLists.txt`, `fetch-upstream.sh`,
`tests/`) is part of this repository and is covered by its licence:
**Apache-2.0**.

It links against two third-party works. Neither is vendored in this repository:
both are acquired at a pinned revision by `fetch-upstream.sh` into a directory
outside the working tree, so what is distributed here is a reference to a
revision and a digest, not a copy.

## privacy-filter.cpp — MIT

- Source: <https://github.com/localai-org/privacy-filter.cpp>
- Pinned: commit `735a6c28607ee82afc3a670383f41b55266a3b9a`
- Licence: MIT (the upstream `LICENSE` file)
- Includes its `ggml` submodule, pinned at commit
  `3af5f5760e19a96427f5f7a93b79cbdf3d4b265b` (MIT).

The sidecar is a *client* of this work: it calls the C API in `include/pf.h` and
links the `pf` target built from that revision. The engine ships no model; the
weights are a separate artefact with its own licence, supplied by the operator
and never committed here.

## nlohmann/json — MIT

- Source: <https://github.com/nlohmann/json>
- Pinned: v3.11.3, single header `json.hpp`
- Licence: MIT (the header carries its own notice)
- Digest: `sha256:9bea4c8066ef4a1c206b2be5a36302f8926f7fdc6087af5d20b417d0cf103ea6`

Upstream `privacy-filter.cpp` carries no header-only JSON library, so the wire
format needs one. It is fetched by content digest rather than assumed present on
the host: a system package would be an undocumented dependency, and a tag can be
moved where a digest cannot.

## Model weights

Not covered by this notice and not distributed here. The operator supplies the
GGUF file; its licence is the one published with the weights. The sidecar
reports the digest of whatever it is pointed at, and refuses to start if it does
not match the digest the operator pinned — so the artefact in use is always
identifiable from the process itself.
